[{:db/id 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-46f6694f-8103-554b-a6d3-9a98e8c2973d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-46f6694f-8103-554b-a6d3-9a98e8c2973d" :question/id #uuid "46f6694f-8103-554b-a6d3-9a98e8c2973d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34711" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n\nIII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-375de494-0474-59f2-a5cb-d4f2d3d924b6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-375de494-0474-59f2-a5cb-d4f2d3d924b6" :answer-field/id #uuid "375de494-0474-59f2-a5cb-d4f2d3d924b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-75b5793f-7a42-5e9f-b867-97cb0a94ee05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-75b5793f-7a42-5e9f-b867-97cb0a94ee05" "answer-75750201-9871-5333-9d36-628baad463f0" "answer-59f9131e-98fe-5931-bf40-b384cfc12aca" "answer-008275fa-715e-57ea-bc82-5a6102db2a5d" "answer-856794aa-f420-58cc-9b35-d295a27c06b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75b5793f-7a42-5e9f-b867-97cb0a94ee05" :answer/id #uuid "75b5793f-7a42-5e9f-b867-97cb0a94ee05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75750201-9871-5333-9d36-628baad463f0" :answer/id #uuid "75750201-9871-5333-9d36-628baad463f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59f9131e-98fe-5931-bf40-b384cfc12aca" :answer/id #uuid "59f9131e-98fe-5931-bf40-b384cfc12aca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-008275fa-715e-57ea-bc82-5a6102db2a5d" :answer/id #uuid "008275fa-715e-57ea-bc82-5a6102db2a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-856794aa-f420-58cc-9b35-d295a27c06b4" :answer/id #uuid "856794aa-f420-58cc-9b35-d295a27c06b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119944 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f8d1a00d-2251-5725-a02b-3b2319318fd8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f8d1a00d-2251-5725-a02b-3b2319318fd8" :question/id #uuid "f8d1a00d-2251-5725-a02b-3b2319318fd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126832" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨t+3,\\,1-t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point $P(4,0,1),$ valid for all real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The point $P(4,0,1)$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨4,0,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨t+3,1-t,{t}^{2}⟩ & =⟨4,0,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the components yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}t+3=4 \\\\ 1-t=0 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the first equation, we get $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other equation. Therefore,  $P(4,0,1)$ is at the tip of the vector $r(1).$\n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨1,-1,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point  $P(4,0,1)$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨4,0,1⟩+u⟨1,-1,2⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb45a89e-3bde-5251-b24c-b1bd686d3497"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb45a89e-3bde-5251-b24c-b1bd686d3497" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb45a89e-3bde-5251-b24c-b1bd686d3497" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7c3eb033-52d1-5b96-94b9-64ac07d6af16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3e141537-57e7-5d24-b24a-a74eaabb1717" "answer-35a27e71-b8e5-549e-97ab-d093597bcb5b" "answer-a8a9f5e6-8ed5-5aa2-8980-b3e5d5b6e091" "answer-01f9c607-a00d-5f26-9c10-092b5fb19c5d" "answer-7c3eb033-52d1-5b96-94b9-64ac07d6af16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e141537-57e7-5d24-b24a-a74eaabb1717" :answer/id #uuid "3e141537-57e7-5d24-b24a-a74eaabb1717" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-2,1⟩+u⟨4,-1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35a27e71-b8e5-549e-97ab-d093597bcb5b" :answer/id #uuid "35a27e71-b8e5-549e-97ab-d093597bcb5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,2⟩+u⟨1,-1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8a9f5e6-8ed5-5aa2-8980-b3e5d5b6e091" :answer/id #uuid "a8a9f5e6-8ed5-5aa2-8980-b3e5d5b6e091" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,2⟩+u⟨4,-1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01f9c607-a00d-5f26-9c10-092b5fb19c5d" :answer/id #uuid "01f9c607-a00d-5f26-9c10-092b5fb19c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,0,1⟩+u⟨-2,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c3eb033-52d1-5b96-94b9-64ac07d6af16" :answer/id #uuid "7c3eb033-52d1-5b96-94b9-64ac07d6af16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,0,1⟩+u⟨1,-1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f0553cd0-23ab-5839-b32e-fb9520332a9c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f0553cd0-23ab-5839-b32e-fb9520332a9c" :question/id #uuid "f0553cd0-23ab-5839-b32e-fb9520332a9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-181534" :question/problem "Let $I=N$ and ${S}_{i}=(0,\\frac{2i}{2i-1}),$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}=$" :question/worked-solution "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{{A}_{i}\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${S}_{1}=(0,2)$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${S}_{2}=(0,\\frac{4}{3})$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${S}_{3}=(0,\\frac{6}{5})$\n\n- if $i=4,$ we have ${S}_{4}=(0,\\frac{8}{7})$\n\nand so on.\n\nNotice that as $i$ increases, \n\n- the left endpoint of the intervals is $0$ for all the sets,\n\n- the right endpoint of the intervals is greater than $1$ and approaches $1$ from the right, never reaching it.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}=(0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72992156-232d-5e59-a853-f830c746fc70"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72992156-232d-5e59-a853-f830c746fc70" :answer-field/id #uuid "72992156-232d-5e59-a853-f830c746fc70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8a4ed120-03c1-59d6-a981-4def59b8adad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a4ed120-03c1-59d6-a981-4def59b8adad" "answer-8d70a1cd-4456-5ae3-b1c0-6ff128292655" "answer-d3f58a65-9c0a-5a6d-943e-ddc8a004490c" "answer-62c57b84-928c-5133-b786-712eefb8d26e" "answer-5f9404ea-93a6-52ed-a4d6-367243aa4e24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a4ed120-03c1-59d6-a981-4def59b8adad" :answer/id #uuid "8a4ed120-03c1-59d6-a981-4def59b8adad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d70a1cd-4456-5ae3-b1c0-6ff128292655" :answer/id #uuid "8d70a1cd-4456-5ae3-b1c0-6ff128292655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,2]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3f58a65-9c0a-5a6d-943e-ddc8a004490c" :answer/id #uuid "d3f58a65-9c0a-5a6d-943e-ddc8a004490c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\frac{4}{3}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62c57b84-928c-5133-b786-712eefb8d26e" :answer/id #uuid "62c57b84-928c-5133-b786-712eefb8d26e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f9404ea-93a6-52ed-a4d6-367243aa4e24" :answer/id #uuid "5f9404ea-93a6-52ed-a4d6-367243aa4e24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186305140 :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+12{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n4(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+12(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(12\\beta +12\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-12\\alpha +12\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}12\\alpha +12\\beta =-8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ -12\\alpha +12\\beta =11\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{19}{24},\\beta =\\frac{1}{8}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{19}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+(-\\frac{19}{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(\\frac{1}{8})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-26d80ffd-784b-5cee-95c0-c712aba5c5de" :activity/id #uuid "26d80ffd-784b-5cee-95c0-c712aba5c5de" :activity/title "Quiz 6" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-4e0ba4b6-098e-52a4-8d07-3abaebd61f9d" "step-bfd67c17-3475-580b-bd20-fca8a021b88f" "step-e2bc513d-bf4c-58fb-89b6-b71a9d225e16" "step-e944ef5c-0b09-5365-be49-0201874b1f7b" "step-48656a2f-f00d-59d7-ab86-aed535a53970"] :activity/first-step "step-4e0ba4b6-098e-52a4-8d07-3abaebd61f9d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-4e0ba4b6-098e-52a4-8d07-3abaebd61f9d" :step/id #uuid "4e0ba4b6-098e-52a4-8d07-3abaebd61f9d" :step/content 17592186265816 :step/next "step-bfd67c17-3475-580b-bd20-fca8a021b88f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bfd67c17-3475-580b-bd20-fca8a021b88f" :step/id #uuid "bfd